│ patch_description        │ The original program failed validation because its complex recursive split/group logic    │
│                          │ returned an empty `column_orderings` list, corrupted row-to-column mapping (rows were     │
│                          │ rebuilt via positional assignment in `column_recursion`, losing row identity and mixing   │
│                          │ cells), and appended an "original_index" helper column to the output. The printed output  │
│                          │ shows it running but validation rejects the returned data/orderings.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Fix: replace the whole editable block with a simple, provably-correct algorithm: preserve │
│                          │ every cell and row exactly, optionally honor `col_merge` via the existing                 │
│                          │ `merging_columns` base method, then evaluate up to three cheap global column-order        │
│                          │ candidates (original order, frequency/length-weighted order, and a distinct-count order)  │
│                          │ by scoring each with the true ideal character-Trie reuse objective (sum of adjacent LCPs  │
│                          │ over sorted serialized rows, using C-speed prefix-slice binary search). Return the best   │
│                          │ order applied uniformly, with a valid per-row column-orderings list of the correct        │
│                          │ length. Row order is preserved (trie reuse is insertion-order independent), dtype is      │
│                          │ preserved via `copy()`.                                                                   │
