│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ rewrite_trie_prefix_reorder                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The failed program relied on broken heuristics: it returned empty column_orderings,       │
│                          │ mutated/merged data via ad-hoc recursion with `itertuples` attribute lookups (wrong for   │
│                          │ arbitrary column names), thread pools that corrupted row assignment (`as_completed` wrote │
│                          │ results to arbitrary positions), and a bogus "sort by first column" step that broke row   │
│                          │ identity. None of it matched the actual objective: maximizing character-Trie prefix reuse │
│                          │ over serialized rows.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix replaces the whole body with a clean, correct implementation:                     │
│                          │ - Serialize each cell exactly like the evaluator (`fillna("")`-style then `str`), once,   │
│                          │ keeping raw values untouched.                                                             │
│                          │ - Build up to three bounded candidate per-row column orderings: (1) global order ranked   │
│                          │ by length-weighted repetition `len(v)*count*(count-1)` with low-cardinality tie-breaks,   │
│                          │ (2) an alternative global ranking, (3) a bounded conditional partition tree (pick the     │
│                          │ field with the largest length-weighted pair repetition inside each group, partition rows  │
│                          │ by its value, recurse with depth/group limits).                                           │
│                          │ - Honor one_way_dep by locking constrained columns into a fixed topological order, honor  │
│                          │ col_merge via the parent `merging_columns` when available, and bound work with            │
│                          │ row_stop/col_stop/early_stop.                                                             │
│                          │ - Score each candidate with the true serial-Trie objective (sorted-string adjacent-LCP    │
│                          │ sum, using C-speed slice-equality binary search instead of per-character loops) and       │
│                          │ return the best, with the original cell values permuted per row and a consistent per-row  │
│                          │ column ordering. Row order and values are preserved; no fabrication, printing, or         │
│                          │ evaluator access.                                                                         │
