│                          │ empty column_orderings list (evaluator requires per-row column orderings consistent with  │
│                          │ returned data), its heavy recursive code with mutable global state (self.val_len,         │
│                          │ dep_graph, lru_caches) could crash or alter data (Counter over mixed types raises on      │
│                          │ unhashable values, grouping/asserts on mismatched shapes, "original_index" column         │
│                          │ manipulation, DataFrame column renaming bugs). The rewrite replaces all of that with a    │
│                          │ simple, safe algorithm: serialize cells once (object dtype preserved), compute a global   │
│                          │ column order ranked by length-weighted repetition (len * count * (count-1)), produce      │
│                          │ per-row column orderings, sort rows lexicographically by serialized row string to         │
│                          │ maximize trie prefix reuse, and return a copy with identical values/shape. Handles        │
│                          │ col_merge by keeping merged columns adjacent in every row ordering. No missing-value      │
│                          │ fabrication, no asserts, bounded runtime.                                                 │
