│ patch_name               │ serial_trie_reuse_rewrite                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The previous implementation was fundamentally broken for the actual objective: it         │
│                          │ returned an empty `column_orderings` list (invalid per-row orderings),                    │
│                          │ fabricated/reconstructed rows via `result_df.loc` with mismatched indices and a           │
│                          │ `pd.DataFrame(columns=...)` skeleton, inserted a fake `original_index` column, mutated    │
│                          │ `group.iloc[:, ...]` slices without effect, and its shape/merge assertions could fail (as │
│                          │ seen in the stdout, the recursion ran but produced invalid output). It also optimized     │
│                          │ squared field lengths and value-count heuristics rather than actual character-Trie prefix │
│                          │ reuse.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Fix: complete rewrite. Cells are serialized exactly as the evaluator does (missing -> "", │
│                          │ else str). Two bounded candidate constructions are built and scored with the true         │
│                          │ serial-Trie objective (sorted-string adjacent LCP sum, binary-search LCP in C-speed       │
│                          │ slices):                                                                                  │
│                          │ 1. A global frequency-ranked column order scoring sum(len(v)*count*(count-1)).            │
│                          │ 2. A conditional partition tree using precomputed factorized integer codes: inside each   │
│                          │ group pick the field with max (count-1)*len savings, partition, recurse with bounded      │
│                          │ depth, using the global order as deterministic tail.                                      │
│                          │ The candidate with the higher measured LCP reuse wins; per-row column orderings are       │
│                          │ returned consistent with the permuted cell data. col_merge is honored via the parent's    │
│                          │ merging_columns with a safe fallback; all values, rows and columns are preserved (object  │
│                          │ dtype output).                                                                            │
