│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ rewrite_lcp_candidate_selection                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The previous program was fundamentally broken: it added an "original_index" column to the │
│                          │ data, returned empty column_orderings (invalid per-row orderings), used fragile           │
│                          │ Counter-based value arithmetic that fails on mixed-type/unhashable cells, built result    │
│                          │ frames via `result_df.loc` on empty DataFrames (never populating rows correctly), and its │
│                          │ assertions on shapes failed (e.g., final shape mismatch when discarding columns). None of │
│                          │ its machinery actually targeted the real objective (serial character-Trie reuse).         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix replaces the whole editable block with a correct, bounded algorithm:              │
│                          │ - Serialize each cell exactly as the evaluator does ("" for missing, str otherwise) for   │
│                          │ scoring only, preserving stored values.                                                   │
│                          │ - Build up to three cheap candidate constructions: (1) global column order ranked by      │
│                          │ sum(len(v)*count*(count-1)), (2) a rank ignoring length, (3) a conditional partition tree │
│                          │ over integer factorization codes choosing split columns by length-weighted pair           │
│                          │ repetition, with bounded depth/candidates and a deterministic global-rank tail.           │
│                          │ - Score each candidate with the exact ideal Trie objective (sum of adjacent LCPs of       │
│                          │ sorted serialized rows, computed with C-speed binary-search prefix comparisons, identical │
│                          │ strings handled directly).                                                                │
│                          │ - Return the best candidate as a per-row permuted DataFrame (object dtype) with valid     │
│                          │ per-row column orderings; all rows/values preserved. col_merge is honored via the         │
│                          │ parent's merging_columns when available, and API parameters (early_stop, row_stop,        │
│                          │ col_stop, distinct_value_threshold, parallel) are accepted and used as bounds only.       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
