│ patch_description        │ A different construction pipeline replacing the current one. Instead of only global       │
│                          │ frequency ranking plus one recursive (k*(k-1))-repetition tree, this version builds three │
│                          │ structurally distinct candidate per-row orderings: (1) a global frequency-ranked order,   │
│                          │ (2) a conditional partition tree whose per-node column gain is the true trie-edge saving  │
│                          │ Σ len·(count−1) (the actual number of shared characters a split saves, not squared        │
│                          │ counts), and (3) a flat two-level clustering variant — rows are split once on their       │
│                          │ highest-entropy column into value groups, and each group receives its own independently   │
│                          │ frequency-ranked global column order (no recursion). All candidates are scored with the   │
│                          │ exact ideal character-trie objective (sum of adjacent LCPs over sorted serialized rows,   │
│                          │ computed with C-speed binary-search prefix comparisons), and the best is returned. The    │
│                          │ diversity of statistics (squared repetition vs edge savings vs entropy-flat-clustering)   │
│                          │ targets the low-scoring dataset where the previous single tree statistic failed, while    │
│                          │ the bounded candidate count keeps runtime comparable or better.                           │
